@page "/founding-groups/rules"
@namespace Ben.Web.Website.Library.Promotions
@inject IBenAdminClient Client

<PageTitle>Founding groups: the rules — IsHaunted</PageTitle>

@*
    The founding groups promotion's rules (Ben, 11/02/2026), in plain words. Every number is read from the
    promotion's settings, so changing one on the admin page changes the rules here too.
*@

<div class="container-fluid px-3 py-4" style="max-width:820px; margin:0 auto;">
    <div class="text-secondary small"><a href="/founding-groups">Founding groups</a></div>
    <h1 class="h3 mb-3">The founding groups rules</h1>

    @if (_loading)
    {
        <BenLoaderOverlay Visible="true" Text="Loading…" />
    }
    else if (_p is not { Showing: true } p)
    {
        <div class="alert alert-secondary">The founding groups promotion isn't open right now.</div>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="founding-rules" data-testid="founding-rules">
            <h2 class="h5">Who can take part</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Any new paranormal investigation group on IsHaunted. Ghost walking tours, paranormal event providers and haunted properties have plans of their own and can't take part.</li>
                <li>A group that already pays for a plan can't take a free one.</li>
                <li>There are @p.Spots spots. A spot is held from the moment a group claims it.</li>
                <li>
                    Spots can be claimed until they're all taken@(p.ClaimsCloseUtc is { } closes ? $" or until {closes:MM/dd/yyyy}, whichever comes first" : "").
                    If a group's week ends without enough members, its spot opens again.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="h5">The week to gather your members</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Your group has @p.GatherDays days from claiming its spot to gather its members.</li>
                <li>
                    A member counts once they've <strong>confirmed their email address</strong>, and only if they're new to
                    IsHaunted or not a member of any other group when they join.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Each person counts for <strong>one group only</strong>. Somebody counted for one founding group can't be
                    counted for another, and can't start a second free group.
                </li>
                <li>A member who leaves the group during its week stops counting.</li>
                <li>
                    When the @p.GatherDays days are up, a group with @p.MinimumMembers or more members counted starts its free
                    @(p.FreeMonths == 12 ? "year" : $"{p.FreeMonths} months"). A group with fewer gives its spot back.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="h5">The free plan</h2>
            <ul>
                @foreach (var plan in p.Plans)
                {
                    <li>@(plan.MaxMembers is { } max ? $"{plan.MinMembers} to {max}" : $"{plan.MinMembers} or more") members: <strong>@plan.Name</strong>.</li>
                }
                <li>The plan is free for @Months(p.FreeMonths) from the day the week ends. No card is needed.</li>
                <li>If your group grows during those months, it moves up to the plan its new size earns, still free. It never moves down.</li>
                <li>
                    When the free time ends, choose your plan on your group's billing page to keep it, at its normal price.
                    We'll write a month and a week before. If it isn't paid, the plan keeps going for two weeks and then stops;
                    nothing you've made is lost.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="h5">The score</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Each group is scored on its own twelve months, from the day its free plan starts.</li>
                <li>
                    Points: @p.PointsPerSession for each field session with at least @p.MinimumReadingsPerSession readings;
                    @p.PointsPerInvestigation for each investigation of your group's, for each member who was there;
                    @p.PointsPerEvidence for each piece of evidence a member offered that was accepted;
                    @p.PointsPerEvent for each event your group hosted that happened;
                    and @p.PointsPerReferral for each group you referred that paid for its plan.
                </li>
                <li>A group's score is its points divided by its members with confirmed email addresses.</li>
                <li>Your group's administrators see every member's points and the group's; each member sees their own.</li>
                <li>
                    The leaderboard shows points per member per month so far, so groups that started at different times compare
                    fairly. It appears once a second group has started its free plan.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="h5">Prizes</h2>
            <ul>
                @if (p.GroupOfTheMonthMonths > 0)
                {
                    <li>
                        <strong>Group of the month:</strong> each calendar month, the founding group with the best score per member
                        that month earns @Months(p.GroupOfTheMonthMonths) free. A group can't win two months running.
                    </li>
                }
                @if (p.ReachedScoreMonths > 0)
                {
                    <li>
                        <strong>Reach the score:</strong> any group with @p.ReachableScorePerMember or more points per member at the
                        end of its twelve months earns @Months(p.ReachedScoreMonths) free.
                    </li>
                }
                @if (p.Winners > 0)
                {
                    <li>
                        <strong>The top @p.Winners:</strong> once claims are closed and every founding group has finished its twelve
                        months, the @p.Winners with the most points per member win @Months(p.WinnerMonths) free, from then. A tie goes
                        to the group with more points in all, then to the group whose free plan started first.
                    </li>
                }
                <li>Free months are added to your plan: a free plan runs that much longer, and a paid plan's next renewal comes that much later.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="h5">Referrals</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>On its billing page, a group can name the group that told it about IsHaunted.</li>
                <li>
                    When that group first pays for its plan, and the payment has stood for two weeks, the group it named earns
                    one free month. That's one month for each group referred, whatever the size of either.
                </li>
                <li>A group can't name itself, or a group with the same owner or administrators. The name is fixed once it has paid.</li>
                <li>Referrals count for every group on IsHaunted, not only the founding groups.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="h5">Fair play</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>We may take a group out of the promotion for making up members or activity. We'll tell it why.</li>
                <li>If we change a number in these rules, the change applies from then on, never to what a group has already earned.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    private FoundingGroupsPublicRecord? _p;
    private bool _loading = true;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        _p = (await Client.GetFoundingGroupsAsync()).Item;
        _loading = false;
    }

    private static string Months(int n) => n == 12 ? "a year" : n == 1 ? "1 month" : $"{n} months";
}
